e 4 has \\\\\\\"bright\\\\\\\". Check other lines — no other \\\\\\\"bright\\\\\\\". Good.\\\\n\\\\nCheck first letters: S, T, E, M, Y. ✓\\\\n\\\\nLine 5 first letter: \\\\\\\"Next\\\\\\\" — N. Wait, Y is needed! Line 5 must start with Y.\\\\n\\\\nRedo line 5 starting with Y, 8 words, ending with \\\\\\\"you\\\\\\\":\\\\n\\\\\\\"Your eyes see this wonder whenever rain and sun...\\\\\\\" Hmm, needs to end with \\\\\\\"you\\\\\\\".\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\"Yet the sky saves this colorful gift just for you.\\\\\\\" Count: Yet(1) the(2) sky(3) saves(4) this(5) colorful(6) gift(7) just(8) for(9) you(10). 10 words.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\"You can chase this wonder whenever rain shines near you.\\\\\\\" Count: You(1) can(2) chase(3) this(4) wonder(5) whenever(6) rain(7) shines(8) near(9) you(10). 10.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\"You can see this wonder whenever rain shines near you.\\\\\\\" Same count, 10.\\\\n\\\\nNeed 8 words: \\\\\\\"You can see this wonder whenever rain...\\\\\\\" Hmm.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\"You will see one whenever sun meets rain near you.\\\\\\\" Count: You(1) will(2) see(3) one(4) whenever(5) sun(6) meets(7) rain(8) near(9) you(10). 10.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\"You can spot one whenever sun meets rain near you.\\\\\\\" 10 again.\\\\n\\\\n8 words: \\\\\\\"You can spot one whenever sun meets rain.\\\\\\\" That's 8 but doesn't end with \\\\\\\"you\\\\\\\". Ends with \\\\\\\"rain\\\\\\\".\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\"You can spot one whenever rain shines near you.\\\\\\\" Count: You(1) can(2) spot(3) one(4) whenever(5) rain(6) shines(7) near(8) you(9). 9. One too many.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\"You can spot one whenever rain shines by you.\\\\\\\" Hmm awkward. 9 words still: You(1) can(2) spot(3) one(4) whenever(5) rain(6) shines(7) by(8) you(9). 9.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\"You can spot one whenever rain falls near you.\\\\\\\" 9.\\\\n\\\\nDrop a word: \\\\\\\"You can spot one whenever rain falls near.\\\\\\\" Doesn't end with you.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\"You can spot one whenever rain shines around you.\\\\\\\" 9.\\\\n\\\\n\\\