at number)\\\\n\\\\n2. **Milo sits in a seat neighbouring Vera.**  \\\\n   → |Milo - Vera| = 1\\\\n\\\\n3. **Milo also sits in a seat neighbouring Soren.**  \\\\n   → |Milo - Soren| = 1\\\\n\\\\n4. **Dina sits in the first or last seat.**  \\\\n   → Dina = 1 or 7\\\\n\\\\n5. **Soren sits in the first or last seat.**  \\\\n   → Soren = 1 or 7\\\\n\\\\n6. **Pia sits somewhere between Milo and Gail.**  \\\\n   → Pia is between Milo and Gail (not necessarily adjacent). So either Milo < Pia < Gail or Gail < Pia < Milo.\\\\n\\\\n7. **Pia also sits somewhere between Gail and Dara.**  \\\\n   → Pia is between Gail and Dara. So either Gail < Pia < Dara or Dara < Pia < Gail.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nLet’s denote the seats:  \\\\n1 2 3 4 5 6 7\\\\n\\\\nWe need to assign each person to a seat.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Step 1: Dina and Soren are in first or last seat.\\\\n\\\\nSo Dina ∈ {1,7}, Soren ∈ {1,7}\\\\n\\\\nBut there are only two end seats: 1 and 7.\\\\n\\\\nSo Dina and Soren must be in seats 1 and 7, in some order.\\\\n\\\\nSo possibilities:\\\\n\\\\n- Dina = 1, Soren = 7  \\\\n- Dina = 7, Soren = 1\\\\n\\\\nLet’s consider both cases.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Case 1: Dina = 1, Soren = 7\\\\n\\\\nThen from clue 1: Vera is to the left of Dina → Vera < Dina = 1 → Vera < 1 → impossible.\\\\n\\\\nSo Vera cannot be to the left of Dina if Dina is in seat 1.\\\\n\\\\nTherefore, **Case 1 is invalid**.\\\\n\\\\nSo Dina cannot be in seat 1.\\\\n\\\\nThus, Dina must be in seat 7.\\\\n\\\\nThen Soren must be in seat 1 (since Soren is in first or last, and 7 is taken by Dina).\\\\n\\\\nSo:\\\\n\\\\n- Dina = 7  \\\\n- Soren = 1\\\\n\\\\nNow, clue 1: Vera is to the left of Dina → Vera < 7 → Vera ∈ {1,2,3,4,5,6}\\\\n\\\\nBut Soren is in 1, so Vera ≠ 1 → Vera ∈ {2,3,4,5,6}\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nNow, clue 2: Milo is next to Vera → |Milo - Vera| = 1\\\\n\\\\nClue 3: Milo is next to Soren → |Milo - Soren| = 1\\\\n\\\\nSoren is in seat 1 → so Milo must be in seat 2 (since only seat 2 is adja