s seat1-seat7: Soren, Milo, Vera, Dara, Pia, Gail, Dina.\\\\n\\\\nNeed final with answer tags only maybe. Ensure no extra? User asks give order between tags. We can just output.\\\"},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"stop\\\",\\\"logprobs\\\":null,\\\"matched_stop\\\":154827}],\\\"model\\\":\\\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\\\",\\\"created\\\":1794483273,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"prompt_tokens\\\":190,\\\"total_tokens\\\":929,\\\"completion_tokens\\\":739,\\\"prompt_tokens_details\\\":{\\\"cached_tokens\\\":0},\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":716,\\\"completion_tokens_details\\\":{\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":716}}}\",\"signature\":{\"text\":\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:1ccab31b1e8029c737605d927335c885007e198b304427fe6890a312d4e0d131:c000f47f052311315a7e5fa02d3e50eb6766f01968887f3b02ca5bd1d550396f\",\"signature\":\"0x7e3f8f17efcfb997a06463d4cc67a682985701f96a41e139076c39a17a7e1b785ec6d0eaf3bd2677590568a2c536fcb1e142772da2048e73592dcbb1c0ad262f1b\",\"signing_address\":\"0x3b753b4406613c5e70ae640508632b600424fa0c\",\"signing_algo\":\"ecdsa\",\"signature_kind\":\"provider_tee\"},\"verdict\":{\"ok\":true}},{\"task\":3,\"model\":\"Qwen/Qwen3-VL-30B-A3B-Instruct\",\"response\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"chatcmpl-dfebf1dc-10d0-48d6-9fc8-e8a2b5199438\\\",\\\"object\\\":\\\"chat.completion\\\",\\\"choices\\\":[{\\\"index\\\":0,\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"We are given a logic puzzle involving six people: **Cleo, Quin, Sami, Iris, Cyrus, and Fern**, sitting in a row of six seats numbered 1 to 6 from left to right.\\\\n\\\\nWe need to determine the order of the people from seat 1 to seat 6, satisfying all the conditions.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Step 1: List the conditions\\\\n\\\\nLet’s restate the clues clearly:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Cleo sits in a seat neighbouring Quin.**  \\\\n   → |Cleo - Quin| = 1\\\\n\\\\n2. **Sami sits in a seat neighbouring Cleo.**  \\\\n   → |Sami - Cleo| = 1\\\\n\\\\n3. **Cleo sits somewhere to the left of Iris.**  \\\\n   → Cleo < Iris (in seat number)\\\\n\\\\n4. **Cyrus sits somewhere between Iris and Sami.**  \\\\n   → Iris and Sami are on opposite sides of Cyrus, so either Iris < Cyrus < Sami or Sami < Cyrus < Iris\\\\n\\\\n5. **Quin sits somewhere between Cyrus and Sami.**  \\\\n   → Cyrus and Sami are on opposite sides of Quin, so either Cyrus < Quin < Sami or Sami < Quin < Cyrus\\\\n\\\\n6. **Fern sits in a seat neighbouring Quin.**  \\\\n   → |Fern - Quin| = 1\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nWe have 6 people: Cleo, Quin, Sami, Iris, Cyrus, Fern.\\\\n\\\\nLet’s denote the seats:  \\\\n1 — 2 — 3 — 4 — 5 — 6\\\\n\\\\nWe need to assign each person to a seat.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### Step 2: Use the chain of adjacency\\\\n\\\\nFrom (1) and (2):  \\\\n- Cleo is adjacent to Quin  \\\\n- Cleo is adjacent to Sami  \\\\n\\\\nSo Cleo is adjacent to both Quin and Sami. That means Cleo is between Quin and Sami, or Quin and Sami are on either side of Cleo.\\\\n\\\\nSo the three people: Quin, Cleo, Sami must be in a block of three consecutive seats, with Cleo in the middle.\\\\n\\\\nSo possible arrangements for (Quin, Cleo, Sami) or (Sami, Cleo, Quin) in three consecutive seats.\\\\n\\\\nSo the trio must be:  \\\\n- Quin - Cleo - Sami  \\\\n- Sami - Cleo - Quin  \\\\n\\\\n(Only these two orders, since Cleo must be adjacent to both.)\\\\n\\\\nSo Cleo is in the middle of Quin and Sami.\\\\n\\\\nLet’s call this the **Cleo block**: Quin-Cleo-Sami or Sami-Cleo-Quin.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\nNow, from (3): Cleo is to the left of Iris → Cleo < Iris\\\\n\\\\nSo Iris is to the right of Cleo.\\\\n\\\\nFrom (4): Cyrus is between Iris and Sami → So Iris and Sami are on opposite sides of Cyrus.\\\\n\\\\nSo either:\\\\n- Iris < Cyrus < Sami\\\\n- Sami < Cyrus < Iris\\\\n\\\\nBut from (3), Cleo < Iris.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, from (5): Quin is between Cyrus and Sami → So Cyrus and Sami are on opposite sides of Quin.\\\\n\\\\nSo either:\\\\n- Cyrus < Quin < Sami\\\\n- Sami < Quin < Cyrus\\\\n\\\\nNow, let’s consider the two possible orders for the Cleo block.\\\\n\\\\n---\\