rus in remaining two seats, with inequalities/between.\\\\n\\\\nConditions:\\\\nCleo left of Iris. So Iris to right of C.\\\\nCyrus between Iris and Sami.\\\\nQuin between Cyrus and Sami.\\\\n\\\\nLet's denote positions. Need include block.\\\\n\\\\nCase A block = S,C,Q,F consecutive in that order. Positions maybe start k=1..3? length4. S at k, C k+1, Q k+2, F k+3. Remaining seats for Iris,Cyrus are the two seats not in block. Need C (Cleo) < Iris. Since Cleo at k+1. Iris must be to right. Remaining seats depend.\\\\n\\\\nAlso Quin between Cyrus and Sami: Q pos k+2 strictly between Cyrus and Sami pos k. Since Sami left of Q. For Q to be between Cyrus and Sami, Cyrus must be right of Q (because between Sami and Cyrus). So Cyrus > k+2. Iris also > k+1. Cyrus between Iris and Sami: Sami at k, Q? Need Cyrus strictly between Iris and Sami. Since Sami left. Thus Cyrus > k and < Iris. So Iris > Cyrus. Combined Cyrus > Q > Sami, Iris > Cyrus. So order Sami < Quin < Cyrus < Iris. Also Cleo at k+1 < Iris okay. Remaining two seats must be to right of Q? Since Cyrus and Iris both > Q. In length4 block, remaining seats maybe before block and after block. Need both remaining seats > Q? Let's check k possibilities:\\\\nk=1: block seats1-4 S,C,Q,F; remaining seats5,6 both >Q pos3. Assign Cyrus pos5, Iris pos6 (since Iris>Cyrus). Conditions: Cyrus between Iris(6) and Sami(1): pos5 yes; Quin(3) between Cyrus(5) and Sami(1): pos3 yes. Works. Order S,C,Q,F,Cyrus,Iris = Sami, Cleo, Quin, Fern, Cyrus, Iris.\\\\nk=2: block seats2-5; remaining seats1,6. Need Cyrus and Iris > Q pos4? Cyrus >4 and Iris > Cyrus, only seat6 for Cyrus\\\"},\\\"finish_reason\\\":\\\"length\\\",\\\"logprobs\\\":null}],\\\"model\\\":\\\"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\\\",\\\"created\\\":1794483274,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"prompt_tokens\\\":180,\\\"total_tokens\\\":1180,\\\"completion_tokens\\\":1000,\\\"prompt_tokens_details\\\":null,\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":0,\\\"completion_tokens_details\\\":{\\\"reasoning_tokens\\\":0}}}\",\"sig